r the 2023-2026 Service Plans and Budgets. See <a href=\"https://www.calgary.ca/service-lines/2023-2026-city-services/waste-recycling.html?service-line-budget-bar-chart-serviceplanbudget-xview=2023&service-line-budget-bar-chart-serviceplan", "last_updated": "2026-05-13", "columns": ["year", "residential_waste_generated_through_black_blue_and_green_cart_programs_kilograms_per_household_", "waste_collection_interruptions_per_10_000_scheduled_stops", "greenhouse_gas_ghg_emission_reduction_from_landfill_gas_management_tonnes_co2e_thousands_", "residential_waste_diverted", "citizens_who_are_satisfied_with_the_job_the_city_is_doing_providing_waste_and_recycling_services_per_cent_"]}, {"id": "yjvm-qkfs", "name": "2026 Q1 Progress Report - Performance Measures", "description": "The City of Calgary's 2026 Q1 Progress Update provides an overview of our achievements and challenges as we continue implementing the 2023-2026 Service Plans and Budgets.", "last_updated": "2026-09-03", "columns": ["target", "story_behind_the_number", "_2024_value", "_2023_value", "_2022_value", "performance_measure_name", "q1_2026_value", "_2025_value", "council_priority_area"]}, {"id": "4y62-crsf", "name": "2026 Q2 Progress Report - Performance Measures", "description": "The City of Calgary's 2026 Q2 Progress Update provides an overview of our achievements and challenges as we continue implementing the 2023-2026 Service Plans and Budgets.", "last_updated": "2026-08-24", "columns": ["performance_measure_name", "_2022_value", "_2023_value", "_2024_value", "_2025_value", "q1_2026_value", "q2_2026_value", "target", "story_behind_the_number", "council_priority_area"]}, {"id": "2tzz-grag", "name": "2024 Mid-Year Progress Report - Performance Measures", "description": "The City of Calgary's 2024 Mid-Year Progress Update provides an overview of our achievements and challenges during the first half of the year as we continue implementing the 2023-2026 Service Plans and Budgets.\n\n- Performance measures - details on how actual performance compares against the Council-approved expected future performance.", "last_updated": "2024-10-30", "columns": ["performance_measure_index", "alignment_with_council", "_2024_value", "performance_measure_name", "level_of_alignment", "_2023_value", "expected_future_value", "performance_measure_status", "story_behind_the_number", "approved_by_service_director", "service"]}, {"id": "f39w-zwp3", "name": "2025 Year-End Progress Report - Performance Measures", "description": "The City of Calgary's 2025 Year-End Progress Update provides an overview of our achievements and challenges as we continue implementing the 2023-2026 Service Plans and Budgets.\n\n- Performance measures - details on how actual performance compares against the Council-approved expected future performance.", "last_updated": "2026-02-23", "columns": ["q4_2025_value", "story_behind_the_number", "q3_2025_value", "target", "_2025_value", "q2_2025_value", "council_priority_area", "_2022_value", "q1_2025_value", "performance_measure_name", "_2023_value", "_2024_value"]}, {"id": "pwur-wvcq", "name": "2015-2018 Operating Budget (Approved November 2014)", "description": "City of Calgary Operating Budget by Department. These values are from the approved budget as at November 2014, and do not reflect budget adjustments or organizational changes since that date.\r\n\r\nThe complete approved Action Plan 2015-2018 (<a href=\"http://www.calgary.ca/CA/fs/Documents/Action-Plan/Approved/Action-Plan-2015-2018-Complete-Approved.pdf\">PDF</a>) is on Calgary.ca", "last_updated": "2018-02-01", "columns": ["status", "department", "recoveries", "year", "revenues", "net_budget", "expenditures"]}, {"id": "x7ai-b6uj", "name": "2024 Mid-Year Progress Report - Initiatives", "description": "The City of Calgary's 2024 Mid-Year Progress Update provides an overview of our achievements and challenges during the first half of the year as we continue implementing the 2023-2026 Service Plans and Budgets.\n\n- Initiatives - details on how the service initiatives are progressing against the plan along with each initiative's alignment with Council's priority areas and impact area.", "last_updated": "2024-11-05", "columns": ["impact_area_table", "impact_type", "funding_type", "alignment_with_council", "initiative_index", "initiative_update", "service", "service_improvement_initiative", "initiative_status", "initiative_name", "approved_by_service_director"]}, {"id": "sizs-hgef", "name": "Road Construction Projects", "description": "Transportation Infrastructure (TI) is responsible for many of the major road construction projects that take place in Calgary. Major road construction projects include construction of new roadways, rehabilitation and upgrades to existing roadways, intersection upgrades, and installation of interchanges.\n\nOther road construction projects taking place in Calgary may be the responsibility of the Road", "last_updated": "2026-11-12", "columns": ["point", "completion", "url", "budget", "title", "description", "projecttype"]}, {"id": "bjag-w7zi", "name": "Traffic Volumes for 2023", "description": "Average Daily Weekday Traffic (ADWT) is the average number of vehicles in 24 hours adjusted for seasonal variation to represent the average weekday. The number on this map represents two-way totals.\nVolume on Provincial roads are provided by Alberta Transportation as a Weighted Average Annual Daily Traffic(WAADT).\nThis traffic flow map is intended to be a general representation of traffic volumes ", "last_updated": "2024-06-17", "columns": ["section", "shape_length", "year", "volume", "section_name", "collection", "multilinestring"]}], "search_population": [], "search_assess_hist": [{"id": "4ur7-wsgc", "name": "Historical Property Assessments (Parcel)", "description": "The historical assessed values of residential, non-residential and farm land properties in Calgary. The properties in this dataset consist of Calgary lands that have a registered parcel at Alberta\u2019s Land Titles Office. Properties that are on The City of Calgary\u2019s annual property assessment rolls, but excluded from this dataset, are titled parking stalls, titled storage units, machinery & equipment", "last_updated": "2026-06-06", "columns": ["land_size_sm", "sub_property_use", "assessment_class", "assessment_class_description", "multipolygon", "comm_name", "year_of_construction", "land_use_designation", "re_assessed_value", "land_size_sf", "roll_number", "address", "assessed_value", "comm_code", "property_type", "nr_assessed_value", "roll_year", "land_size_ac", "cpid", "fl_assessed_value"]}]}